    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d306">

                <pb facs="0382" n="370" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg370"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.0040/826: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-06-17">June 17, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1571. Your 2763, June 17. Department’s 994, April 20 and 1402, June l.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d306-f1"/> Your 1635, April 21<anchor n="2" xml:id="d306-f2"/>
                    and 2558, June 7.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d306-f3"/> In view of assurances of
                    safe-conduct given by German Government and all other belligerent governments
                    for “the several voyages of <hi rendition="#italic">Drottningholm</hi> between
                    New York and Lisbon” and for “the several voyages of <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gripsholm</hi> between New York and Lourenço Marques”, the United States
                    Government cannot accept German Government’s statement “that <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Drottningholm</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gripsholm</hi> must not touch” a so-called “extended zone of
                    operations”.</p>
                <p>United States Government awaits confirmation from German Government that German
                    assurances of safe-conduct for <hi rendition="#italic">Drottningholm</hi> and
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Gripsholm</hi> remain valid as originally given.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d306-f1" n="1" xml:id="d306-f1-content">
                <p>Neither printed. Telegram No. 1402 contained instructions to request the Swiss
                    Government to obtain assurances of safe-conduct from all Axis Governments for
                    the several voyages of the <hi rendition="#italic">Gripsholm</hi> between New
                    York and Lourenço Marques (701.0090/156).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d306-f2" n="2" xml:id="d306-f2-content">
                <p>See footnote 83, <ref target="#pg360">p. 360</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d306-f3" n="3" xml:id="d306-f3-content">
                <p>Not printed; it conveyed German assurances of safe-conduct for the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gripsholm</hi> from New York to Lourenço Marques and
                    return (701.0090/246).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
